{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of the plan — is it to maximize the total annual net income (crops + dairy cows + chickens + external work earnings), or is it to maximize only the farm production income (crops + animals) while external work is just a way to use leftover labor?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response presents a single binary choice regarding the optimization objective, which constitutes one semantically independent clarification question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say total annual net income from the farm's operations, does that include the earnings from external work (2.1 yuan/person-day in spring/summer, 1.8 yuan/person-day in autumn/winter) as part of the income to be maximized, or is external work only a way to dispose of leftover labor that doesn't count toward the objective?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether external work earnings are included in the objective function or treated as a constraint/disposal mechanism."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "How much land does one hectare of each crop (soybean, corn, wheat) require per year — is it exactly 1 hectare per hectare planted, i.e., the crop variables are simply the hectares planted of each crop?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the land requirement definition for the crop variables."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The 100-hectare land limit — does it apply to the sum of crop hectares plus the 1.5 hectares of feed land per dairy cow, or is the 1.5 hectares of feed land per cow taken from a separate land pool outside the 100 hectares?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy clarification regarding how the 100-hectare limit interacts with the feed land allocation, presenting two mutually exclusive options for one decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The 15,000-yuan investment limit — does it cover only the animals (400 yuan per dairy cow + 3 yuan per chicken), or does it also include any investment for crops or other farm activities?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question about the scope of the investment limit, presenting a binary choice (animals only vs. animals plus crops/other activities) that constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the labor constraints, is the total person-days used (crops + animals + external work) in each season required to be at most the available amount (3,500 in autumn/winter, 4,000 in spring/summer), with any unused labor simply left idle and not counted as income?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single compound clarification question asking for confirmation of the labor constraint logic and the treatment of unused labor. Since it seeks a single policy confirmation regarding the constraint and its consequence, it counts as one independent question."
}

